        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="1082" n="1052" xml:id="pg1052"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.014 Antarctic/10–1347</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chilean Embassy to the Department of State </hi>
                </head>
                <p>In view of the interest of the Government of Chile in matters pertaining to the
                    Antarctic Region, and with the desire to continue her policy of close
                    understanding with the United States on this subject initiated in 1939, there
                    exists a desire to learn the thought of the United States with reference to: <list>
                        <label>1)</label>
                        <item>the possible convocation of an Antarctic Conference;</item>
                        <label>2)</label>
                        <item>the possible territorial claims of the United States in the Antarctic;
                            and</item>
                        <label>3)</label>
                        <item>whether such claims might include Marguerite Bay, situated within the
                            boundaries of the Chilean Antarctic.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Information would be appreciated, also, with reference to the expedition to the
                    Antarctic announced by the United States Navy to take place at the end of 1947,
                    particularly if it is intended for it to extend to Marguerite Bay, and other
                    places within the Chilean Antarctic Territory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-13">13 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >October</hi> 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
